WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — latency (30s) Narrator Daniel

1
00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:07.927
Research papers routinely demonstrate tenfold cheaper inference months or years before mainstream products adopt them.

2
00:00:08.347 --> 00:00:10.999
Part of the lag is systems integration,

3
00:00:10.999 --> 00:00:16.982
and part is quantized by quarterly reporting, funding rounds, and hardware depreciation.

4
00:00:17.402 --> 00:00:22.351
Public filings show most of a task's dollar cost is amortizing the machine,

5
00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:24.660
not the kilowatt-hours at the plug.

6
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:33.056
Once execution gets cheap, vendors charge for switching friction—and coding automation tools collapse that moat.
